Subject: Keep Wiggler's first-frame health at 0 on JP and US

AVOID_UB sets Wiggler's health to 4 in his init, as EU does, because his
first frame of acceleration reads it before anything sets it. That read is
not undefined: every object field is zeroed when the object spawns (natively
as on the N64), so JP and US read 0 and accelerate accordingly. Only EU sets
it. Found auditing AVOID_UB (docs/avoid_ub.md).

--- a/src/game/behaviors/wiggler.inc.c
+++ b/src/game/behaviors/wiggler.inc.c
@@ -150,7 +150,9 @@
         cur_obj_unhide();
     }
 
-#if defined(VERSION_EU) || defined(AVOID_UB)
+// Not undefined on JP and US: object fields are zeroed when the object is
+// spawned, so Wiggler's first frame of acceleration reads a health of 0.
+#if defined(VERSION_EU)
     o->oHealth = 4; // This fixes Wiggler reading UB on his first frame of his acceleration, as his health is not set.
 #endif
 }
